  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Crisis at the Idol Awards and the Aftermath of Victory</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Gwi-Ma wants to take over the surface world no matter what. He believes that with help from the Saja Boys, led by Jinu, he can triumph over the Huntrix girls and their new allies from beyond the stars. Will his plan be successful? Or will Rumi, Zoey, Mira, Glimmer, Bow, Catra, and Adora succeed in turning the Honmoon golden and sealing it forever, permanently trapping Gwi-Ma and all demons in the underworld, regardless of the consequences? You'll have to read to find out the results of this epic battle and what happens to the Huntrix girls, and their newfound friends, in the days, weeks, and months afterward, including a dramatic revelation from Rumi's mother-of-sorts, Celine, which partially explains why she treated Rumi the way she did...&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>lefemmerouge</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
